WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:04.640
Hey youtubers it's Charlie and this week was
the final episode of season 4.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:09.130
The title of the episode was the ch and it
aired on Father's Day which is just brilliant

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:10.640
planning in my mind.

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:13.850
There's so much we need to talk about but
first here's the details on my giveaway.

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:15.990
Just as a way to say thank you to all you
guys for being so awesome this season I'm

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:16.990
tripling the giveaway.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:20.110
I'm picking three random subscribers from
the comments on this video.

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:22.650
It's just a twenty dollar amazon giftcard.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:26.400
I'll announce the winners in my Q&amp;A video
tomorrow.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.190
Because so many of you asked for a super long
finale video I compromised and instead of

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:33.930
focusing on 5 really big WTF moments I'm doing
10.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:34.930
Then I'll do my review.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:39.199
I'll briefly mention some season 5 stuff,
but I'm doing a separate predictions video

00:00:39.199 --> 00:00:40.629
tomorrow.

00:00:40.629 --> 00:00:43.690
Careful for spoilers if you haven't seen the
episode yet, but here we go.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:48.190
Number 10 - Jon and Mance Drink to dearly
departed Gingers

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:49.839
Mance is such an interesting character.

00:00:49.839 --> 00:00:51.660
And he knows Jon Snow better than he knows
himself.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.940
In case you didn't catch it last season.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:57.251
Mance used to be a brother of the Night's
Watch, so he knows all their tricks and that

00:00:57.251 --> 00:01:00.409
they have nothing left.

00:01:00.409 --> 00:01:06.260
So this negotiation was more about him getting
Jon to believe that they really did just want

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:11.340
to hide behind the Wall before the White Walker
army marched on the Haunted Forest.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:13.580
That was where they were, the Haunted Forest.

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:17.690
It's right near where the Weirwood Jon took
his Oath and Ygritte's body to dust.

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:20.390
Number 9 - Stannis Attacks The Wildlings

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:21.580
This was such an awesome reveal.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:25.501
I'd seen all the teasers for the episode but
for some reason my brain still though, white

00:01:25.501 --> 00:01:27.570
walkers, when the horn blew.

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:30.200
It was definitely one of the best special
effects shots in the episode.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:34.940
In case you've never played it, the opening
title sequence for the show pays homage to

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:39.090
the Song of Ice and Fire board game with all
the minatures.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:44.710
So when they panned out all I could think
of was that and that they were thematically

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:49.170
calling out the title of book 3 Storm of Swords
with the swarm of men charging in from both

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:50.170
sides.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:54.020
I did get really excited when the camera panned
left and you saw the formations on the opposite

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:55.070
side of the Haunted Forest.

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:57.310
It was like watching a slow moving train wreck.

00:01:57.310 --> 00:01:59.950
It's a really terrible act but you can't look
away.

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:03.180
I'd say that's a good metaphor for the entire
episode.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:04.770
A slow moving train wreck you can't stop watching.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:06.390
It's just too amazing to look away.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:10.939
Number 8 - Qyburn Saves The Mountain
I'm a huge fan of Frankenstein and Bride of

00:02:10.939 --> 00:02:15.180
Frankenstein so using Qybryn and The Mountain
as analoges for those characters is so much

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:16.180
fun.

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:19.909
Those films are such big touchstones for hollywood
film makers I always love it when directors

00:02:19.909 --> 00:02:20.959
pay homage to them.

00:02:20.959 --> 00:02:25.549
Like when Pycelle said it was his 'laboratory'
and referenced the fact Qyburn had been thrown

00:02:25.549 --> 00:02:28.550
out of the citadel for experimenting with
Necromancy.

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:33.010
It's not necromancy like the magic the white
walkers use, Qyburn does it using chemistry.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:38.450
It looks like he was in the process of transfusing
the Manticore Poisoned blood out of the Mountain,

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:40.650
but we don't know what he's going to replace
it with.

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:44.180
That's something we can talk more about in
my Season 5 predictions video.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:53.719
If you've read the books please use the spoiler
tag when commenting about the mountain please.

00:02:53.719 --> 00:02:57.480
Number 7 - Cersei Throws Twincest In Tywin's
Face

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:01.620
The biggest surprise of this scene was the
genuine wtf face Tywin made.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:05.019
I always thought that he knew what was really
going on and just chose to not let on.

00:03:05.019 --> 00:03:08.109
Like he was too proud to let any outrage show.

00:03:08.109 --> 00:03:13.180
Cersei's threat was that she would tell everyone
about her relationship with Jaime if Tywin

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:14.180
forced her down the aisle.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:18.480
I think she was more motivated by her love
of Tommen than her desire to not get married

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:19.480
again.

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:21.329
But yeah, she really didn't want to be married
to anyone.

00:03:21.329 --> 00:03:25.160
Even if there weren't any social restrictions
about sisterwiving I feel like she would choose

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:26.480
to not marry Jaime.

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:29.731
To be fair though, the Targaryens married
brother to sister for the entire history of

00:03:29.731 --> 00:03:30.731
their family.

00:03:30.731 --> 00:03:34.299
I think people didn't call them out on it
as much because they had dragons to barbecue

00:03:34.299 --> 00:03:35.299
any critics.

00:03:35.299 --> 00:03:39.629
It happened directly after with Jaime, but
who else noticed that he was reading the White

00:03:39.629 --> 00:03:40.629
Book when Cersei and he started to have sex.

00:03:40.629 --> 00:03:43.900
He even pushed it off the table like it was
a glass of wine.

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:48.370
The White Book is a literary representation
of the honorable deeds previous Kingsguard

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:49.390
brothers have done.

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:53.309
So by casting it off the table, Jaime was
throwing away his honor again.

00:03:53.309 --> 00:03:57.519
It's like Cersei is his heroin and he's been
trying to quit all season and just can't do

00:03:57.519 --> 00:03:58.519
it.

00:03:58.519 --> 00:04:00.719
Number 6 - Daenerys has to Chain The Dragons
Up

00:04:00.719 --> 00:04:04.689
Anyone who has had to crate train a puppy
will understand how sad this was.

00:04:04.689 --> 00:04:09.999
As many WTF moments as there were, this was
one of the only ones I didn't cheer for.

00:04:09.999 --> 00:04:11.949
This was something that happened in the books.

00:04:11.949 --> 00:04:15.760
Drogon starts to kill people while he's hunting.

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:18.700
The little girl who's bones we saw probably
wasn't the target.

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:20.940
It's not like Drogon is going after people.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:25.820
She was just standing in the middle of a flock
of goats when he came to eat them.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:30.250
Viserion and Rhaegal are the only ones that
get chained up because Drogon is roaming free

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:31.550
all over the countryside.

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:34.950
So we won't see him again till next season.

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:38.310
Number 5 - Jon Burns Ygritte under the weirwood
(only cry worthy moment)

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:42.040
This actually reminded me a little of Return
of the Jedi when Luke burned his father Darth

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:43.650
Vader's body in the forest.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:46.550
That tree was the same weirwood where he took
his night's watch oath.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:49.590
I loved how she was eulogized be several different
characters.

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:52.950
Like everyone recognized how amazing she was
and how much she loved Jon in her own special

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:53.950
way.

00:04:53.950 --> 00:04:56.630
I hope someday we get to see Rose Leslie and
Kit Harington work together on a movie or

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:59.400
another tv show.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:03.510
Number 4 - Bran Meets The Three Eyed Raven
and The Children of the Forest

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:06.000
This felt like one of the most important events
on the show.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.620
Like Bran was being crowned King of the forest.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:11.250
Like Luke Skywalker meeting Yoda for the first
time.

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:15.000
Yoda always knew Luke would come to learn
from him just like the Three Eyed Raven had

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.970
been watching Bran and all the other characters
their whole lives.

00:05:17.970 --> 00:05:21.150
If you didn't catch it, when he said I've
had many names, it was a big reference to

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:23.930
his life before he became the last greenseer.

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:27.960
When he was alive he was a Targaryen Bastard
named the Bloodraven.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:32.300
He was the son of Aegon the Fourth, the king
that precipitated the Blackfyre Rebellion.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:35.870
I did a bonus video for the Bloodraven a little
while ago so I'll put a link in the description

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:37.400
for it if you want to learn more about that
character.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:41.230
But I could do a whole video for Bran at the
Weirwood.

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:44.090
The homage to Ray Harryhausen with the skeleton
warriors.

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:46.030
That's from Clash of the Titans.

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:49.780
Harryhausen was this really famous visual
effects creator who's style looked just like

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:50.780
this.

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:54.320
He just did it with real life models because
it was before the age of digital effects.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:55.920
The Children of the Forest are part of the
show now.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:58.510
And they have crazy power so I can't wait
to see how Bran's story unfolds as it relates

00:05:58.510 --> 00:06:02.350
to both them and the greenseer.

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:05.740
Number 3 - Brienne Vs The Hound

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:07.570
This was one of the biggest changes from the
books.

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:13.330
But he was killed by people seeking the bounty
on his head.

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:18.590
They also didn't do the Lady Stoneheart character,
which is who Brienne ran into in the books.

00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:22.560
So because they got rid of these two big plot
points they had to do the shootout at the

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:29.210
OK Vale Corral between Brienne and The Hound
to reign in their stories.

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:32.740
Just like with Craster's house earlier this
season.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:36.680
You see big scenes added that weren't in the
books because of changes they made to things

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:37.680
a long time ago.

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:38.930
It's like the butterfly effect.

00:06:38.930 --> 00:06:41.790
The changes get bigger as we get further along
in the story.

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:46.660
So either they roll with it or they do Hound
v Brienne to pull it back closer to the book

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:47.660
story.

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:49.790
Number 2 - Arya refuses to Kill the Hound

00:06:49.790 --> 00:06:52.790
Arya is so cold now it's hard to read her
emotions.

00:06:52.790 --> 00:06:56.101
I think she knew the Hound was just trying
to goad her into mercy killing him.

00:06:56.101 --> 00:07:00.190
And because he couldn't read her, he just
kept escalating things trying to find the

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:08.030
thing that would make her so mad she'd do
it.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:12.650
I love that she didn't.

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:14.960
It shows that she's even darker than you thought.

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:16.450
Remember where the heart is Arya.

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:17.900
You're headed to Braavos.

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:24.350
The coin scene was right out of the books.

00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:29.910
It should be noted that she did try to join
Jon at the Wall.

00:07:29.910 --> 00:07:35.780
They kept Braavos in the opening credits so
I was pretty sure they were going to do that

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:37.690
plot from the books.

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:41.940
I also did a Braavos video that I'll add as
a link in the description if you want to learn

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:42.940
more about the city.

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:43.940
It's one of the coolest new places we'll see
next year.

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:48.580
and my Number 1 WTF moment - Tyrion Kills
Tywin and Shae.

00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:51.770
Their whole relationship distilled in three
minutes.

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:55.860
There are so many things that stand out about
this.

00:07:55.860 --> 00:08:00.290
The way Tyrion left Jaime was a huge change
from the books.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:04.090
I'd say it was as big of a change as the Brienne
Hound scene.

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:07.570
In the books when Jaime frees Tyrion he tells
him that his first wife was never a whore

00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:09.350
and Tywin just cast her out.

00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:11.340
So out of rage Tyrion lies and says he really
did kill Joffrey and leaves saying he hates

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:12.340
his whole family including Jaime.

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:13.350
Like he despises them all.

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:17.340
The change allows the show to hold on to that
brotherly bond between them.

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:21.150
Jaime and Tyrion will always love each other
as opposed to the books where tyrion hates

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:22.150
everyone.

00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:27.480
It was a change I was really happy with.

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:30.650
The Shae scene was pretty close to the books
too.

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:34.479
He chokes her with his father's gold chain
of office, the chain that the hand of the

00:08:34.479 --> 00:08:35.479
king wears.

00:08:35.479 --> 00:08:38.779
They showed the chain dangling but it was
hard to see if you weren't looking for it.

00:08:38.779 --> 00:08:42.730
Who else really liked that Peter Dinklage
let the crossbow drag on the ground as he

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:43.730
walked down the hallway.

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:46.310
Their talk was really good and for a minute
I actually did believe Tywin when he said

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:49.840
he'd never let Tyrion be killed.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:52.120
But my favorite moment was the reload.

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:57.930
Not Tywin's words, just Tyrion casually reloading
the crossbow and shooting him again.

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:04.540
Now it's your turn though.

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:08.190
Let me know what your favorite moment from
the episode was and if there were any big

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:10.090
surprises you didn't see coming.

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:14.450
I know on a show like this that's based on
books it's really hard to not get spoiled,

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:18.490
but I was still surprised by Brienne and the
Hound's scene and Stannis arriving at the

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:19.529
wall.

00:09:19.529 --> 00:09:24.980
Overall I gave the episode an A plus for being
my new favorite game of thrones finale.

00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:28.780
The way they change the plot helped keep it
from being too predictable even if there were

00:09:28.780 --> 00:09:33.050
some big book moments and I can't stop thinking
about that fight scene between Brienne and

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:34.050
The Hound.

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:37.291
I'm actually wondering if that scene was part
of the reason Gwendoline Christie was cast

00:09:37.291 --> 00:09:40.050
in Star Wars.

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:44.070
That was almost a better fight than Oberyn
Martell versus the Mountain.

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:47.360
It's hard to pick one actor as delivering
the best performance in the episode.

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:54.090
I'll say Peter Dinklage and Lena Headey really
stood out which isn't a surprise.

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:57.800
Maisie Williams is going to be someone you
all need to watch closely next season.

00:09:57.800 --> 00:09:59.060
She just keeps getting better and better.

00:09:59.060 --> 00:10:00.480
Sophie Turner too, but Sansa wasn't even in
this episode.

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:04.260
Rory McCann had the best death of the episode
and possibly the season.

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:08.390
Let me know if you think any other character
had a better death this season.

00:10:08.390 --> 00:10:11.690
I know we didn't see him die, it just ended
with him yelling at Arya.

00:10:11.690 --> 00:10:14.160
But I don't think he's coming back next year.

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:18.500
I didn't mention it in my top 10 moments,
but Arya and Brienne bonding over being tomboys

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:19.820
was so much fun.

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:22.500
I love the way the show plays with your expectations.

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:26.340
I thought she'd be the one to go after the
Hound, but it was Arya and the Hound that

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:28.980
went after her for thinking she was on the
Lannister payroll.

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:32.890
And who among us can say we do not also want
a valyrian blade?

00:10:32.890 --> 00:10:38.390
I'm going to dedicate a separate video to
Season 5 predictions and plot lines but things

00:10:38.390 --> 00:10:43.010
that they pretty clearly foreshadowed were
The Mountain turning into Frankenstein's Monster,

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:47.720
Arya going to Braavos, Bran with the greenseer
and Stannis at the Wall.

00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:48.720
Be sure to subscribe to get that video.

00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:50.620
I'll be posting it monday and then my Q&amp;A
video.

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:54.890
Later this week I'll do one more bonus video
and then after that I'll just being doing

00:10:54.890 --> 00:10:56.670
one bonus video a week every Sunday.

00:10:56.670 --> 00:11:01.550
So we can still do Game of Thrones' Sundays
until Season 5 gets here next April.

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:05.770
Right now click here for the Q&amp;A and Click
here for my Season 5 predictions.

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:08.080
I'll add the annotations as soon as I post
them.

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:12.330
Thanks for watching, now everyone go re-watch
the episode.

00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:16.450
High Fives!

